    <h2 class="pd-title">Contingency &amp; Prize Insurance</h2>
    <section class="pd-broker-note" aria-label="Insurance broker note">
      <div class="pd-broker-icon" aria-hidden="true">⚖</div>
      <div class="pd-broker-body">
        <span class="pd-broker-tag">From a licensed insurance broker</span>
        <p class="pd-broker-text">
          <strong>N2N Insurance Brokerage</strong> does not represent any single insurer — it <strong>independently represents the client</strong>
          as an FSS-registered broker (Reg. No. 2026-012201). We compare the wordings, rates and service of AIG · Chubb · DB · Hyundai · KB · Meritz
          to propose the <strong>cover and price best suited to your risk</strong>. Each insurer's full wording is provided at application and binding.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
    <div class="pd-tabs" role="tablist">
      <button class="pd-tab-btn active" data-tab="tab1" role="tab">Overview</button>
      <button class="pd-tab-btn" data-tab="tab2" role="tab">Cover</button>
      <button class="pd-tab-btn" data-tab="tab3" role="tab">How to apply</button>
    </div>

    <section id="tab1" class="pd-tab-pane active" role="tabpanel">
<div class="pd-section"><h3>Overview</h3>
        <p>Contingency insurance covers the risk that a promotional or prize event triggers a <strong>large payout</strong> — a winner claims a high-value prize, a lucky-draw is won, or redemptions exceed forecast. The insured pays a fixed premium and the insurer funds the prize if the agreed trigger occurs.</p></div>
      <div class="pd-section"><h3>Key features</h3>
        <ul class="pd-feature-list">
          <li><span class="pd-num">01</span><div class="pd-ftext"><strong>Fixed premium</strong>
            <p>A known premium replaces an uncertain prize liability.</p></div></li>
          <li><span class="pd-num">02</span><div class="pd-ftext"><strong>Prize / over-redemption</strong>
            <p>Prize indemnity and over-redemption beyond forecast.</p></div></li>
          <li><span class="pd-num">03</span><div class="pd-ftext"><strong>Predictable budget</strong>
            <p>Marketing spend becomes predictable.</p></div></li>
          <li><span class="pd-num">04</span><div class="pd-ftext"><strong>Tailored mechanic</strong>
            <p>Structured to the specific promotion rules.</p></div></li>
        </ul></div>
      <div class="pd-section"><h3>Who needs it</h3>
        <ul class="pd-feature-list">
          <li><span class="pd-num">01</span><div class="pd-ftext"><strong>Brands &amp; advertisers</strong>
            <p>Companies running prize promotions.</p></div></li>
          <li><span class="pd-num">02</span><div class="pd-ftext"><strong>Retail &amp; e-commerce</strong>
            <p>Lucky-draw and redemption campaigns.</p></div></li>
          <li><span class="pd-num">03</span><div class="pd-ftext"><strong>Event &amp; sports organizers</strong>
            <p>Hole-in-one and prize competitions.</p></div></li>
          <li><span class="pd-num">04</span><div class="pd-ftext"><strong>Agencies</strong>
            <p>Agencies structuring client promotions.</p></div></li>
        </ul></div>
    </section>
    <section id="tab2" class="pd-tab-pane" role="tabpanel">
<div class="pd-section"><h3>Main losses covered</h3>
        <ul class="pd-bul">
          <li>Indemnity for the prize or payout when the defined trigger occurs</li>
          <li>Over-redemption costs beyond the agreed forecast</li>
          <li>Defined prize competitions (e.g. hole-in-one)</li>
        </ul></div>
      <div class="pd-section"><h3>Main endorsements</h3>
        <ul class="pd-feature-list">
          <li><span class="pd-num">01</span><div class="pd-ftext"><strong>Hole-in-one</strong>
            <p>Cover for a specified hole-in-one prize.</p></div></li>
          <li><span class="pd-num">02</span><div class="pd-ftext"><strong>Weather-contingent prize</strong>
            <p>Prize triggered by a weather condition.</p></div></li>
          <li><span class="pd-num">03</span><div class="pd-ftext"><strong>Multiple winners</strong>
            <p>Cover where more than one winner is possible.</p></div></li>
        </ul></div>
      <div class="pd-exclude"><h4>Main exclusions</h4>
        <ul>
          <li>Fraud, collusion or manipulation of the result</li>
          <li>Triggers set incorrectly or outside the agreed rules</li>
          <li>Events or prizes outside the documented promotion structure</li>
          <li>Prizes already won or in progress at inception</li>
          <li>Taxes and costs outside the insured prize</li>
        </ul></div>
    </section>
    <section id="tab3" class="pd-tab-pane" role="tabpanel">
<div class="pd-section"><h3>Conditions &amp; process</h3>
        <ul class="pd-bul">
          <li>The promotion mechanic and prize value drive the structure</li>
          <li>Rules and verification process are agreed at inception</li>
          <li>Independent adjudication may be required for high-value prizes</li>
        </ul></div>
      <div class="pd-section"><h3>What we need to quote</h3>
        <ul class="pd-feature-list">
          <li><span class="pd-num">01</span><div class="pd-ftext"><strong>Promotion rules</strong>
            <p>The mechanic, odds and prize structure.</p></div></li>
          <li><span class="pd-num">02</span><div class="pd-ftext"><strong>Prize value</strong>
            <p>Value and number of prizes at risk.</p></div></li>
          <li><span class="pd-num">03</span><div class="pd-ftext"><strong>Participation</strong>
            <p>Expected entries and campaign dates.</p></div></li>
          <li><span class="pd-num">04</span><div class="pd-ftext"><strong>History</strong>
            <p>Prior promotions and any past payouts.</p></div></li>
        </ul></div>
      <div class="pd-section"><h3>Other notes</h3>
        <ul class="pd-bul">
          <li>Verification and adjudication conditions apply to claims</li>
          <li>Final terms and premium are confirmed after insurer underwriting</li>
        </ul></div>
    </section>

